untable"], "examples": ["Aren't we full of dash this morning?"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["energy", "vim", "vitality"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(Nigeria, Ghana, Liberia, countable, uncountable) A bribe or gratuity; a gift.", "tags": ["Nigeria", "countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The traditional practice of offering gifts or \"dash\" to chiefs has often been misinterpreted by scholars to provide a cultural explanation for the pervasive incidence of bribery and corruption in modern Africa.", "reference": "1992, George Billy Nii Ayittey, Africa Betrayed, →ISBN, →OCLC, →OL, page 44:"}, {"text": "Writing in 1924 on a similar situation in Ugep, the political officer, Mr. S. T. Harvey noted: \"In the old days there was no specified dowry but merely dashes given to the father-in-law, from 8 to 20 rods according to the status of the man[…]The dowry is made small because whatsoever a woman farms or reaps during her life time is by native custom the property of her parents.\"", "reference": "2006, Adiele Eberechukwu Afigbo, The Abolition of the Slave Trade in Southeastern Nigeria, 1885–1950 (Rochester Studies in African History and the Diaspora; 25), University of Rochester Press, →ISBN, →ISSN, page 99:"}, {"text": "The only other times you'll be asked for a dash is from beggars.", "reference": "2008, Lizzie Williams, updated by Mark Shenley, Nigeria: The Bradt Travel Guide, published 2012, →ISBN, →OCLC, →OL, page 109:"}], "synonyms": ["douceur", "sweetener", "backhander", "bribe", "bung", "coffee money", "cold drink money", "dash", "douceur", "inducement", "kopi money", "pay-off", "payola", "subornation", "sweetener", "tea money", "benefaction", "boon", "concession", "donative", "fairing", "gift", "grant", "present", "tithing"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(dated, euphemistic) A stand-in for a censored word, like \"Devil\" or \"damn\". (Compare deuce.)", "tags": ["countable", "dated", "euphemistic", "uncountable"], "examples": ["Sir Thomas looks as if to ask what the dash is that to you! but wanting still to go to India again, and knowing how strong the Newcomes are in Leadenhall Street, he thinks it necessary to be civil to the young cub, and swallows his pride once more into his waistband.\nComment: Some editions leave this passage out. Of those that include it, some change the 'you!' to 'you?'.", "Who the dash is this person whom none of us know? and what the dash does he do here?"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["beep", "blankety-blank"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Ellipsis of dashboard.", "tags": ["abbreviation", "alt of", "countable", "ellipsis", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The dash clock said 2:38 when[…] I turned off a dirt road[…].", "reference": "1955 October 19, Rex Stout, The Next Witness, Three Witnesses, 94 Bantam, →ISBN, page 31:"}], "synonyms": ["control panel", "instrument panel"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": [{"definition": "(Internet, informal) The dashboard of a social media user.", "tags": ["Internet", "countable", "informal", "uncountable"], "examples": ["-i hope you find at least one thing on your dash that will make you laugh today.", "i cannot tell you how happy it makes me when i see my dash filled with selfies from other folks who look like me."], "quotes": [{"text": "“You wanna know what else is all over my dash? Gifs of you and your boyfriend.\"", "reference": "2018, Krista Ritchie, Becca Ritchie, Alphas Like Us, unnumbered page:"}], "synonyms": ["control panel", "instrument panel", "timeline", "feed", "graphical user interface"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}]}, {"definition": "(UK, India) A prime symbol.", "tags": ["India", "UK", "countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["dash"], "